{
 "summary": "Fix integers d ≥ 4 and 2 ≤ n ≤ d−2, and constants C_AD ≥ 1 and C_R ≥ 0. The Lean statement says there exist θ > 0 and M ≥ 0 that work for every regular (Radon) Borel measure μ on ℝ^d satisfying two conditions: n-AD regularity with constant C_AD, and the uniform L² bound C_R for all hard truncations of the kernel (x−y)/|x−y|^{n+1}. For such μ, every x ∈ supp μ and every 0 < r ≤ diam(supp μ) admit an M-Lipschitz map g from the Euclidean n-ball B(0,r) into ℝ^d with μ(B(x,r) ∩ g(B)) ≥ θ rⁿ. This matches the excerpted Theorem 1.3 with class-uniform constants. The main caveat is that Definition 1.2 and condition (1.2) are not in the excerpt, so the exact conventions (μ versus Hⁿ|E, r ≤ diam versus r < diam, open versus closed balls) cannot be fully checked, though each plausible variant is equivalent up to constants.",
 "glossary": [
  {"decl": "Ambient", "line": 10, "plain": "ℝ^d with the Euclidean norm", "standard_concept": "Euclidean space ℝ^d", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": ""},
  {"decl": "AdmissibleRadius", "line": 12, "plain": "0 < r ≤ diam(supp μ), where diam is the extended diameter (∞ allowed; 0 if the support is empty or a single point)", "standard_concept": "admissible scales 0 < r ≤ D_E", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": "Matches the range in (1.4). The degenerate case D_E = 0 makes the conclusion vacuous, as the paper notes."},
  {"decl": "kernel", "line": 15, "plain": "K_n(x−y) = (x−y)/|x−y|^{n+1}, with value 0 on the diagonal (Lean inverse of 0 is 0)", "standard_concept": "n-dimensional Riesz kernel", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": "Any normalizing constant is absorbed into C_R."},
  {"decl": "truncated", "line": 18, "plain": "R_{μ,ε} f(x) = ∫_{|x−y|>ε} f(y) K_n(x−y) dμ(y), as a Bochner integral (equal to 0 if not integrable)", "standard_concept": "hard ε-truncation of the Riesz transform", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": "Lemma 1.4 shows absolute convergence for AD-regular μ with D_E > 0 and f ∈ L², so the junk value does not arise."},
  {"decl": "ADRegularWithConstant", "line": 22, "plain": "C ≥ 1 and, for x ∈ supp μ and 0 < r ≤ diam(supp μ), rⁿ/C ≤ μ(B(x,r)) ≤ C rⁿ, with open balls", "standard_concept": "n-Ahlfors–David regularity", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": "The upper bound is only required at support points and admissible radii; Lemma 1.4 recovers the global bound."},
  {"decl": "RieszL2BoundedWithConstant", "line": 28, "plain": "For all ε > 0 and f ∈ L²(μ): R_{μ,ε} f ∈ L²(μ; ℝ^d) and ‖R_{μ,ε} f‖₂ ≤ C_R ‖f‖₂", "standard_concept": "uniform L² boundedness over hard truncations, condition (1.2)", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": "The text of (1.2) is not in the excerpt; this matches the abstract's description."},
  {"decl": "BallImageConclusion", "line": 34, "plain": "For x ∈ supp μ and 0 < r ≤ diam(supp μ), there is an M-Lipschitz g : B_{ℝⁿ}(0,r) → ℝ^d with μ(B(x,r) ∩ g(B)) ≥ θ rⁿ", "standard_concept": "big pieces of Lipschitz images of balls (uniform rectifiability, Definition 1.2)", "matches_standard": "partly", "note": "Mass is measured by μ rather than possibly Hⁿ|E. These are comparable for AD-regular μ with constants depending on C_AD, n and d. Definition 1.2 is not in the excerpt."},
  {"decl": "QuantitativeFullStatement", "line": 42, "plain": "∀ d, n with 2 ≤ n ≤ d−2 (d ≥ 4), ∀ C_AD ≥ 1, ∀ C_R, ∃ θ > 0, ∃ M, ∀ regular μ that are AD(C_AD) and Riesz(C_R) bounded, the ball-image conclusion holds", "standard_concept": "Theorem 1.3 with constants depending only on d, n, C_AD, C_R", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": ""}
 ],
 "lean_claims": [
  {"theorem": "quantitative_higher_codimension_riesz_rectifiability", "line": 57, "plain": "Let d, n ∈ ℕ with d ≥ 4, n ≥ 2, n+2 ≤ d, and let C_AD ≥ 1 and C_R ≥ 0. Then there exist θ > 0 and M ≥ 0 with the following property. For every regular Borel measure μ on ℝ^d satisfying, for x ∈ supp μ and 0 < r ≤ diam supp μ, the bounds rⁿ/C_AD ≤ μ(B(x,r)) ≤ C_AD rⁿ, and satisfying ‖R_{μ,ε} f‖_{L²(μ)} ≤ C_R ‖f‖_{L²(μ)} with R_{μ,ε} f ∈ L² for all ε > 0 and f ∈ L²(μ): for every such x and r there is an M-Lipschitz g from the open n-ball of radius r into ℝ^d with μ(B(x,r) ∩ g(B)) ≥ θ rⁿ."}
 ],
 "paper_claims": [
  {"ref": "Theorem 1.3", "plain": "For d ≥ 4 and 2 ≤ n ≤ d−2, an n-AD-regular Radon measure on ℝ^d with uniformly L²-bounded hard truncations of the Riesz transform (1.2) is uniformly n-rectifiable (big pieces of Lipschitz images of balls, Definition 1.2), with θ and M depending only on d, n, C_AD and C_R."}
 ],
